    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What the alarm means / what to do",
      "datasource": null,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**The iXon3 buzzer** = a thermal switch on the heat sink has cut power to the TE cooler (iXon3 Hardware Guide §1.3.7). It resets by itself once the head has cooled. Causes: chiller off or low water flow, blocked vents, fan off/low, room above 30 °C.\n\nThe SDK cannot read this switch on the iXon3, and the **CCD sensor temperature looks normal** until the sensor warms up. Watch the **TEC voltage**, the **head temperature** and **sensor − set point**.\n\n**On ALARM:** check the chiller (running, flow, water above the dew point), fan = full, vents. If it repeats, switch the cooler off — repeated trips wear out the thermal switch."
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 38,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 7
      },
      "id": 21
    }
